WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.520
Is HBO's "The Last of Us" the first really&nbsp;
good video game adaptation? Time will tell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.860
but early reviews are uniformly positive.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:12.180
Tension and "The Last of Us" have gone&nbsp;
hand-in-sweaty-controller-holding hand since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:17.940
the original video game masterpiece was released&nbsp;
in 2013. The post-apocalyptic tale of Joel and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:22.380
Ellie's fungus-riddled road trip is one of the&nbsp;
greats and earned the right to be in the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:27.600
conversation as "The Walking Dead" and "Mad Max"&nbsp;
as far as stories set at the end of the world go.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.260
That stress level has been raised&nbsp;
again in the past few weeks in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:36.540
lead-up to HBO's live-action adaptation&nbsp;
— arriving on January 15 — handled by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:40.380
the game's creator, Neil Druckmann,&nbsp;
and "Chernobyl" creator Craig Mazin.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:44.220
Fans have been waiting with great&nbsp;
anticipation to see just how Pedro&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:49.500
Pascal and Bella Ramsey have handled playing&nbsp;
two icons of not just video games but one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.180
the greatest survival horror stories ever&nbsp;
told. Well, now the wait is finally over.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:58.020
Critics have shuffled in online like&nbsp;
Clickers with their final verdicts on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:02.100
the all-new series ahead of its release&nbsp;
this Sunday. Has the unthinkable finally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:05.520
happened? Has "The Last of Us" been&nbsp;
given the treatment it deserves in its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:09.420
transition to live action? By the sounds&nbsp;
of things, it may have even surpassed it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:14.340
as the show is sitting at 100% on Rotten&nbsp;
Tomatoes, as of the making of this video.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.508
Empire gave it a perfect score of 5/5,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.508 --> 00:01:21.120
praising it for accomplishing where&nbsp;
others failed. John Nugent wrote,

00:01:34.655 --> 00:01:38.400
In the game, Ashley Johnson and Troy&nbsp;
Baker are the performers beneath the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:42.960
pixels of Ellie and Joel. Bella Ramsey and&nbsp;
Pedro Pascal are our live-action iterations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:47.100
of the young girl with a big secret and&nbsp;
the father figure forced to protect her.

00:01:47.329 --> 00:01:48.709
"I'm not family?"

00:01:48.709 --> 00:01:51.240
"No. You're cargo."

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:57.300
Admittedly, Pascal playing the reluctant guardian&nbsp;
of a youngster isn't anything new for him given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:02.280
the fact he's been doing it off-world for some&nbsp;
time now as Din Djarin in "The Mandalorian". The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:07.140
real success story, however, looks to be coming&nbsp;
from Ramsey, whose role on "The Last of Us" will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:12.000
undoubtedly demand more of the young star as&nbsp;
the show progresses. Simon Cardy of IGN wrote,

00:02:29.572 --> 00:02:33.240
It turns out, though, that while these might&nbsp;
be winning turns from the show's leads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:35.280
there's a surprise in the supporting cast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:39.060
that might steal the show from them.&nbsp;
Minor spoilers for Episode 3 ahead.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:43.620
As much as Joel and Ellie will try to avoid&nbsp;
strangers and infected stragglers during their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:47.820
journey, "The Last of Us" the game does include&nbsp;
some supporting stars who are willing to help,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:53.460
albeit reluctantly. One fine example is Bill,&nbsp;
the antisocial ally played on the show by Nick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:57.720
Offerman, who shares the screen with his&nbsp;
on-screen love, Frank, played by Murray&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:01.980
Bartlett of "The White Lotus." According to&nbsp;
Daniel Fienberg of the Hollywood Reporter,

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:20.700
Something that's only briefly hinted&nbsp;
at in the game, Bill and Frank's time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.400
together is seemingly brought&nbsp;
to the forefront in the show.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:27.300
If it does yield a nomination or two come&nbsp;
awards season, by the sounds of things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.720
it wouldn't be the only one for "The&nbsp;
Last of Us." One of the best games&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:34.692
ever made might have just become&nbsp;
one of the best shows of 2023.

